----- stdout -----
Initialize a new Pina program project.

Creates a buildable program scaffold with Pina dependencies, source layout, and a starter instruction. Existing scaffold files are preserved unless --force is supplied.

Usage: pina init [OPTIONS] <NAME>

Arguments:
  <NAME>
          Rust package name for the new program, for example `counter_program`

Options:
  -p, --path <DIR>
          Target directory. Defaults to `./<name>`

      --force
          Overwrite scaffold files that already exist

      --sbpf-linker
          Experimental: scaffold for the upstream sbpf-linker toolchain.
          
          Records `sbpf-linker = true` under `[project]` in pina.toml, so every `pina build` compiles for bpfel-unknown-none with the pinned nightly Rust and the sbpf-linker binary instead of cargo-build-sbf; remove the key to revert. The scaffold also carries the static syscall rustflags and a build-program alias for bare cargo builds. The pinned toolchain ships rust-src for build-std; install sbpf-linker separately. The build runs without LTO by design; see docs/sbpf-linker-evaluation.md for the measured caveats.

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Examples:
  pina init counter_program
  pina init counter_program --path ./programs/counter_program
  pina init counter_program --path ./programs/counter_program --force

----- stderr -----
